@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Class structure - Move and reorder story cards
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
set separator none
package "frontend/projects/mission-control" {
  class KanbanBoardPage {
    +workspaceId: Signal<Guid>
    -layout: ProjectLayoutPage
    -moveRequest: WritableSignal<MoveRequest?>
    -chosenMove: WritableSignal<MoveChoice?>
    -decision: WritableSignal<CompletionDecision?>
    -moveStatus: WritableSignal<MoveStatus?>
  }
  note right of KanbanBoardPage
    Opens MoveStoryDialog with moveRequested's
    MoveRequest and UnfinishedTasksDialog when
    moveStatus asks for confirmation; relays dialog
    outputs to BoardView inputs. On Settled and Forbidden
    any open dialog closes itself. Failed (500/503) with no dialog
    open shows the "Couldn't move story" toast with the
    reference ID (Retry sets chosenMove to the status's
    choice); Forbidden (unexpected 403) shows the "Your
    access changed" toast without Retry; a Settled
    announcement shows a success toast. Toasts follow
    moveStatus with or without a dialog. MoveStoryDialog
    close: none (dismissed) clears the request, sends
    nothing, focus to the card's Move button; Settled:
    focus follows the outcome; Forbidden: focus to the
    Move button; ConfirmationRequired: opens
    UnfinishedTasksDialog. UnfinishedTasksDialog close
    (Settled, Forbidden): focus to the card's Move button
    unless a board alert, the board region (story
    deleted), or the not-found heading takes it;
    none (a navigation closed it): relays kept through
    completionDecision, so the pending move ends
    without a request.
    modeChanged calls layout.modeChanged().
    No method calls into BoardView.
  end note
  class ProjectLayoutPage {
    +modeChanged(): void
  }
  note bottom of ProjectLayoutPage
    Defined by projects/manage-workspaces;
    reached through inject(ProjectLayoutPage).
  end note
  class MoveStoryDialog {
    +request: InputSignal<MoveRequest>
    +status: InputSignal<MoveStatus?>
    +chosen: OutputEmitterRef<MoveChoice>
    +close(result: MoveStoryOutcome?): void
  }
  note bottom of MoveStoryDialog
    Reads nothing on open: columns, totals and
    position choices (Top, After each loaded card,
    Bottom) come from request. Holds a choice, not
    a draft: no FormDraft. Closes itself when status
    reports Settled, Forbidden or ConfirmationRequired;
    no result on Cancel, Close or Escape (unavailable
    while a move is pending).
  end note
  class MoveStoryOutcome {
    +kind: Settled | Forbidden | ConfirmationRequired
  }
  class UnfinishedTasksDialog {
    +prompt: InputSignal<CompletionPrompt>
    +confirmed: OutputEmitterRef<StoryCompletionCondition>
    +kept: OutputEmitterRef<void>
    +close(result: UnfinishedTasksOutcome?): void
  }
  note bottom of UnfinishedTasksDialog
    Escape is Keep in progress (kept); never
    dismissed without a choice. Closes itself when
    prompt reports Settled or Forbidden. A navigation
    closes it with no result; the opener relays kept.
  end note
  class UnfinishedTasksOutcome {
    +kind: Settled | Forbidden
  }
  class CompletionPrompt {
    +storyKey: string
    +storyTitle: string
    +savedStatus: WorkStatus
    +condition: StoryCompletionCondition
    +state: Asking | ServerCount | Saving | Failed | Settled | Forbidden
    +referenceId: string?
  }
}
package "frontend/projects/domain" {
  class BoardView {
    +workspaceId: InputSignal<Guid>
    +sprintBoard: InputSignal<boolean>
    +chosenMove: InputSignal<MoveChoice?>
    +completionDecision: InputSignal<CompletionDecision?>
    +moveRequested: OutputEmitterRef<MoveRequest>
    +moveStatus: OutputEmitterRef<MoveStatus>
    +modeChanged: OutputEmitterRef<void>
    -query: WritableSignal<BoardQuery?>
    -board: ResourceRef<BoardResult>
    -acknowledged: WritableSignal<BoardResult?>
    -pendingMove: WritableSignal<MoveStoryCommand?>
    -generation: WritableSignal<int>
  }
  note right of BoardView
    Move members only: the sprint-only outputs
    (removeRequested, sprintLoaded) belong to sprint
    execution, the Kanban-only members to view the board.
    One pending move per board: other moves, drag
    and Load more are aria-disabled until it settles.
    A move start increments the generation and clears
    the query (the resource aborts any read in flight).
    Results stamped with an older generation or
    another board ID are discarded.
    Success sets the query to the loaded window of the
    source and destination columns; the resolved columns
    become the latest acknowledged state.
    Failure restores the latest acknowledged state.
    A board-changed 409 or a 400 refusal restores it,
    ends the move (Settled) and shows a page alert with
    Reload board (no Retry, no reference ID); a 403
    restores it and reports Forbidden.
    A mode-changed 409 restores it, ends the move
    (Settled, no board-changed alert) and emits modeChanged.
    While UnfinishedTasksDialog is open, a 500 or 503
    keeps the move pending and reports Failed.
  end note
  class MoveRequest {
    +card: BoardCard
    +columns: MoveColumn[]
  }
  class MoveColumn {
    +status: WorkStatus
    +totalCount: int
    +loadedCards: MoveColumnCard[]
  }
  class MoveColumnCard {
    +storyId: Guid
    +title: string
  }
  note bottom of MoveColumn
    From the latest acknowledged board;
    totalCount is the server's full count.
  end note
  class MoveChoice {
    +storyId: Guid
    +destination: WorkStatus
    +position: int
  }
  class MoveStatus {
    +state: Saving | ConfirmationRequired | Failed | Forbidden | Settled
    +card: BoardCard
    +choice: MoveChoice
    +condition: StoryCompletionCondition?
    +referenceId: string?
    +message: string?
  }
  note bottom of MoveStatus
    Failed: 500 or 503, always with referenceId.
    message: the failure text (Failed) or the
    success announcement (Settled after a saved
    move); null otherwise. A 400 refusal reports
    Settled; BoardView shows its reason.
  end note
  class CompletionDecision {
    +markDone: bool
    +condition: StoryCompletionCondition?
  }
}
package "frontend/projects/api" {
  interface "ResourceRef<T>" as ResourceRef {
    +value: Signal<T | undefined>
    +status: Signal<loading | resolved | error>
    +error: Signal<unknown>
    +reload(): void
  }
  interface IBoardService {
    +boardResource(query: () => BoardQuery | undefined): ResourceRef<BoardResult>
    +move(command: MoveStoryCommand): Promise<MoveStoryResult>
  }
  class BoardService {
    -http: HttpClient
  }
  interface IToastService {
    +show(toast: Toast): void
  }
}
package "MissionControl.Api" {
  class BoardsController {
    -sender: ISender
  }
}
package "MissionControl.Application" {
  class MoveStoryCommand {
    +workspaceId: Guid
    +storyId: Guid
    +sprintBoardId: Guid?
    +destination: WorkStatus
    +targetPosition: int
    +expectedStoryVersion: long
    +expectedBoardVersion: long
    +completionCondition: StoryCompletionCondition?
  }
  class MoveStoryResult {
    +boardId: Guid
    +storyId: Guid
    +status: WorkStatus
    +position: int
    +storyVersion: long
    +boardVersion: long
  }
  class MoveStoryCommandHandler {
    +handle(request: MoveStoryCommand, ct: CancellationToken): Task<MoveStoryResult>
  }
  class StoryStatusTransition {
    +apply(placements, status, sent?, requestedBoardId?, position?): bool
  }
  note bottom of StoryStatusTransition
    Defined by confirm story completion; shared with
    story edits and the completion endpoint. False
    means confirmation required (nothing changed).
    Otherwise the requested board gets the explicit
    position, other live placements append, and the
    active sprint's version increments for a member.
  end note
  interface IMissionControlDataSession {
    +BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync(workspaceId: Guid, ct: CancellationToken): Task
    +LoadStoryPlacementsAsync(workspaceId: Guid, storyId: Guid, ct: CancellationToken): Task<StoryPlacements?>
    +AddAuditEvent(auditEvent: AuditEvent): void
    +SaveChangesAsync(ct: CancellationToken): Task
  }
  class StoryPlacements {
    +story: WorkItem
    +mode: DeliveryMode
    +boards: IReadOnlyList<BoardState>
    +completion: StoryCompletionCondition
  }
}
package "MissionControl.Domain" {
  class BoardState {
    +id: Guid
    +workspaceId: Guid
    +sprintId: Guid?
    +version: long
  }
  class BoardPlacement {
    +boardId: Guid
    +storyId: Guid
    +status: WorkStatus
    +position: int
    +move(status: WorkStatus, position: int): void
  }
  class StoryCompletionPolicy {
    +requireConfirmation(sent: StoryCompletionCondition?, current: StoryCompletionCondition): bool
  }
  class StoryCompletionCondition {
    +storyVersion: long
    +taskRevision: long
    +unfinishedCount: int
  }
}
package "MissionControl.Infrastructure" {
  class MissionControlDataSession
}
KanbanBoardPage --> BoardView : composes; inputs and outputs only
KanbanBoardPage --> MoveStoryDialog : opens on moveRequested; request input
KanbanBoardPage --> UnfinishedTasksDialog : opens when confirmation is required
KanbanBoardPage ..> CompletionPrompt : builds from moveStatus
MoveStoryDialog ..> MoveStoryOutcome : close result
UnfinishedTasksDialog ..> UnfinishedTasksOutcome : close result
KanbanBoardPage ..> ProjectLayoutPage : modeChanged() on modeChanged
KanbanBoardPage ..> IToastService : inject TOAST_SERVICE; move toasts
BoardView ..> MoveRequest : moveRequested output
MoveRequest *-- MoveColumn
MoveColumn *-- MoveColumnCard
BoardView ..> MoveChoice : chosenMove input
BoardView ..> CompletionDecision : completionDecision input
BoardView ..> MoveStatus : moveStatus output
BoardView ..> IBoardService : inject BOARD_SERVICE
IBoardService <|.. BoardService
IBoardService ..> ResourceRef : returns per consumer
IBoardService ..> MoveStoryCommand : sends
BoardsController ..> MoveStoryCommand : dispatches
MoveStoryCommandHandler ..> MoveStoryCommand : handles
MoveStoryCommandHandler --> MoveStoryResult : returns
MoveStoryCommandHandler --> StoryStatusTransition : status changes through
MoveStoryCommandHandler --> BoardPlacement : same-column reorder
StoryStatusTransition --> StoryCompletionPolicy : checks before any change
StoryStatusTransition --> BoardPlacement : moves every live placement
StoryCompletionPolicy ..> StoryCompletionCondition : compares
BoardState "1" *-- "*" BoardPlacement
MoveStoryCommandHandler ..> IMissionControlDataSession : uses
IMissionControlDataSession ..> StoryPlacements : loads tracked
StoryPlacements --> BoardState
StoryPlacements --> StoryCompletionCondition
IMissionControlDataSession <|.. MissionControlDataSession
MoveStatus -[hidden]down- ResourceRef
UnfinishedTasksDialog -[hidden]down- BoardsController
CompletionPrompt -[hidden]down- MoveStoryCommand
BoardService -[hidden]down- BoardsController

@enduml
